  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You do not go to work.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You do not get your salary.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ You go to work.\n\n- $¬B:$ You get your salary.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you get your salary, then you go to work.",
